# Ir - Ugur interatomic potential, hard truncation, the reference parameters
#
# pair_style ugur
# pair_coeff * * Ir.ugur Ir
#
# Truncation: hard - phi2 does not vanish at rcut2, it stops at -172 meV (6.74 of k_B T at 296 K).  USE for static properties and for lattice dynamics: measured against neutron dispersion the hard sets average 9.5 % over the 29 elements that have one, against 12.7 % for the switched sets, and are closer in 23 of them.  DO NOT use for molecular dynamics: copper, whose step is 8.4 meV, drifts 350 meV/atom/ns in NVE and climbs from 296 K to over 1100 K in 200 ps
# MD: DO NOT USE.  At 600 K the crystal collapses: it reaches 821 K and its potential energy falls below the static lattice.  Static properties from this set are still valid.
#
# LATTICE STABILITY: this set is NOT a harmonic minimum.
# Along the Setyawan-Curtarolo path its frequencies reach -8.1 cm^-1,
# with 0.07 % of the sampled modes imaginary.  That is a separate
# failure from the 600 K screen above and is not covered by it.
#
# Nudge test: FAILED.  Displace every atom by 1e-5 A and relax, and the crystal keeps 8345x that displacement and settles 0.17 meV/atom LOWER.  The reference lattice is not this potential's minimum, so the elastic constants above are the constants of a structure it does not hold.  Static reference only; do not use for defects, surfaces or dynamics.
#
# Fitted to: cohesive energy, lattice constant, bulk modulus and the elastic
# constants of Ir at its experimental lattice constant.  Nothing else.
#
# Format is LAMMPS's Tersoff convention - one line per ordered triple
# (centre, leg, leg) - so that this file and a multi-element one are read the
# same way.  For a single element that is one line.
#
# el1 el2 el3  m D alpha r0 gamma C alpha3 rcut2 rcut3 taper lam2 lam4
Ir Ir Ir 6.0881090870075534 0.99232216566625275 0.32413373234854154 4.0718649451479587 0.01871283801222156 -0.38098383767613142 0.16784786788761014 9.9814000000000007 4.0718743994627342 -1 0 0
